Reject a JBIG2 symbol dictionary that exports more symbols than its input and
new symbols together (SDNUMEXSYMS > SDNUMINSYMS + SDNUMNEWSYMS). The count
sizes JBIG2SymbolDict's bitmap table before the export flags are checked, so a
bogus 32-bit value allocated up to 2^32 entries.

Regression test cpp/tests/poppler-jbig2-exported-symbols-test.cpp decodes a
symbol dictionary without symbols that exports 0xffffffff of them and fails
every operator new above 256 MB (32 GB without the fix).
limit-jbig2-symbol-count, applied after this patch, also caps SDNUMEXSYMS at
65535, so once it is applied the test passes without this fix too.

Not fixed upstream as of 9182fd5.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for SDNUMEXSYMS,
numExSyms, readSymbolDictSeg, JBIG2 symbol dictionary).

